            <ArticleTitle>The laparoscopic appearance of Schistosomiasis may be mistaken for &quot;non-pigmented&quot; endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the case history of a patient with symptoms and signs suggestive of endometriosis, who was found to have Schistosomiasis. The laparoscopic appearance was of gelatinous deposits throughout the pelvis which were thought to be &quot;non-pigmented&quot; endometriosis. However, histological examination of the biopsy specimens revealed Schistosomiasis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
